workedExamples.solution_text:
Start at the origin. For $A$, move $2$ units right, then $5$ units up. For $B$, move $5$ units right, then $2$ units up.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[color={rgb,255:red,204;green,204;blue,204},very thin,xstep=10mm,ystep=10mm] (0,0) grid (6,6);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(6.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,6.4) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \n in {1,...,6}{\draw[black] (\n,0.06)--(\n,-0.06);\draw[black] (0.06,\n)--(-0.06,\n);\path (\n,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\n$};\path (0,\n) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\n$};}
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[->,dashed,color={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255}] (0,0)--(2,0)--(2,5);
\draw[->,dashed,color={rgb,255:red,239;green,96;blue,104}] (0,0)--(5,0)--(5,2);
\fill[black] (2,5) circle (2pt);\path (2,5) node[above right] {$A$};
\fill[black] (5,2) circle (2pt);\path (5,2) node[above right] {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The first coordinate gives the horizontal movement. Reversing the coordinates changes the position.

